    description: "The selection index keeps ids of tests that were renamed or removed, statement_narrow names them among the left-out tests, and the manifest header and CI's echo line count them ('By statement: 2438 test(s) deselected'). On PR #2322 the 327 selected files held 9,895 tests and CI ran 7,510: 2,385 left out, not 2,438. The 53 ids (15 in test_nested_assignment_defines.py, 8 in test_verify_claims_unseeded_ingress.py, 7 in test_verify_claims_untyped_receiver_caveat.py, ...) match no testcase of a whole run of those files. Selection is not affected (an id that matches nothing removes nothing); the reported number is wrong by 2.2%. Fix shapes: drop index rows for tests a complete run of the file no longer collects, or count after matching. Repro: the '#- ' lines of .ci/affected-tests.txt at b735e10fe against the junit of 'smart-test --no-by-statement <its 327 files>'. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/kunah/ (ci_pytest_2322.log, file_level_local.log)."  # bf3f
